WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.773 --> 00:00:06.300
Priya Raman: Morning, Lauren. How's Friday treating you over there?

2
00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:14.618
Lauren Whitfield: Busy. We had two clinics short-staffed this week, so I'm just now catching up on everything else. How about you?

3
00:00:15.447 --> 00:00:22.963
Priya Raman: Same kind of week. I pulled the numbers before this, so I have them if you want to start there.

4
00:00:24.114 --> 00:00:25.336
Lauren Whitfield: Yeah, go ahead.

5
00:00:26.112 --> 00:00:35.770
Priya Raman: September came in around 41,500 calls across the 38 clinics, up about 6 percent from August. Central scheduling is still carrying the biggest share of that.

6
00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:41.824
Lauren Whitfield: That tracks. We added two schedulers in mid-September, which is part of the bump.

7
00:00:42.037 --> 00:00:45.546
Priya Raman: Good to know. Anything on the Genesys side misbehaving?

8
00:00:45.808 --> 00:00:50.777
Lauren Whitfield: No, routing has been steady. PreSense pops are landing fine for the agents.

9
00:00:51.944 --> 00:00:56.402
Priya Raman: Great. Redaction is on the agenda, as usual. Anything new there?

10
00:00:57.327 --> 00:01:06.078
Lauren Whitfield: Actually, yes. Legal finished their review of the BAA last week, and it kicked up a question I need to bring to you.

11
00:01:06.437 --> 00:01:08.531
Priya Raman: Sure, what are they asking?

12
00:01:09.518 --> 00:01:23.878
Lauren Whitfield: So right now redaction is all or nothing across transcripts and summaries, and legal wants us to be able to choose which identifiers get masked, like dates of birth or member IDs, and keep some fields visible for certain roles.

13
00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:29.482
Priya Raman: Okay. And who would need to see the unmasked version?

14
00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:40.043
Lauren Whitfield: Compliance and our quality team, probably. Not front-line staff. And they want a record of who viewed what, so we can show it in an audit.

15
00:01:41.271 --> 00:01:48.904
Priya Raman: Got it. Is this something legal flagged as required before they'll sign off on anything, or more of a gap they want closed?

16
00:01:49.938 --> 00:02:00.940
Lauren Whitfield: More of a gap. Nobody's blocking us. But they put it in writing, so I'd rather get ahead of it than explain later why we didn't ask.

17
00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:11.688
Priya Raman: That makes sense. I'll write it up as a request with the legal context. Can I tell the team this came out of the BAA review?

18
00:02:12.836 --> 00:02:17.854
Lauren Whitfield: Please do. That'll help them understand why it's not just a preference.

19
00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:26.328
Priya Raman: And would role-based access need to line up with how permissions work in Genesys or Salesforce, or would this live on its own?

20
00:02:27.595 --> 00:02:33.959
Lauren Whitfield: I don't know yet. Let me check with our compliance lead before I answer that.

21
00:02:34.339 --> 00:02:37.100
Priya Raman: Fine. Anything else from legal while we're here?

22
00:02:38.026 --> 00:02:42.274
Lauren Whitfield: No, that's the only item. Everything else came back clean.

23
00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:53.770
Priya Raman: Good. Last thing on my list, we're due to review the QM scorecards next month. Do you want to keep that on the calendar or move it?

24
00:02:54.554 --> 00:03:03.511
Lauren Whitfield: Keep it. The quality leads have been asking about it. Can we push it to the second week? First week is our flu shot ramp.

25
00:03:04.957 --> 00:03:13.912
Priya Raman: Second week works. I'll send an invite and add the redaction item as a separate line so it doesn't get buried.

26
00:03:14.784 --> 00:03:16.027
Lauren Whitfield: Perfect. Thanks, Priya.

27
00:03:16.797 --> 00:03:18.681
Priya Raman: Thanks, Lauren. Talk next week.
